/*
Problem: Count the Number of Special Characters I (LC 3120)
Topic: String / Hashing

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

A character is "special" if both its
lowercase and uppercase forms appear
in the string.

Use two boolean arrays:

• lower[i] stores whether
  ('a' + i) exists.

• upper[i] stores whether
  ('A' + i) exists.

Finally, count the indices where both
arrays contain true.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. Create two boolean arrays of
   size 26.

2. Traverse the string.

   • If lowercase, mark it in lower.

   • If uppercase, mark it in upper.

3. Traverse all 26 letters.

4. Count indices where both arrays
   are true.

5. Return the count.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

"aAbBc"

lower:

a b c

upper:

A B

Common letters:

a, b

Answer:

2

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

"abc"

Only lowercase letters exist.

Answer:

0

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

Each position in the boolean arrays
represents one alphabet letter.

If both lowercase and uppercase
versions are marked, that character
is special.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n)

One pass over the string and one pass
over the 26 letters.

Overall: O(n)

Space : O(1)

Two fixed-size arrays of length 26.

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

String Hashing / Frequency Tracking
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int numberOfSpecialChars(string word) {

        vector<bool> lower(26, false);
        vector<bool> upper(26, false);

        int count = 0;

        // Record existing characters
        for (char ch : word) {

            if (islower(ch))
                lower[ch - 'a'] = true;

            else
                upper[ch - 'A'] = true;
        }

        // Count letters present in both forms
        for (int i = 0; i < 26; i++) {

            if (lower[i] && upper[i])
                count++;
        }

        return count;
    }
};
